# A built bundle, if `Scripts/install.sh Release .` ever puts one here. The
# script installs to /Applications by default and takes a directory as its
# second argument, and the repository root is the obvious thing to type. The
# bundle does not belong in history: git stores Mach-O whole rather than as a
# delta, so every rebuild committed would be another full copy kept forever,
# and a binary that has gone stale shows no diff to say so. The zip a release
# is cut from is the same object under another name.
/MUTHUR.app/
/MUTHUR.zip

# cdda2wav's leavings. It writes these beside itself, into whatever directory it
# was run from, and §19 is worked by hand from the repository root — so they land
# here and a `git add -A` takes them. Named exactly and anchored to the root
# rather than `audio*`, which would one day swallow real material. Two digits
# because a CD holds at most 99 tracks.
/audio.cddb
/audio.cdindex
/audio.cdtext
/audio_[0-9][0-9].inf
